{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "op": "ANSWER",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_trend", "cumulative_mrr_trend"],
      "text": "Monthly net new MRR has been moving $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.direction across 2024, gaining roughly $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month on an OLS fit, while cumulative MRR has followed a $finding:cumulative_mrr_trend.direction trajectory at $finding:cumulative_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month — together signaling that the business is adding more recurring revenue than it is losing over the period."
    },
    {
      "op": "EXPLAIN",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_trend", "cumulative_mrr_trend", "net_new_mrr_current_state", "net_new_mrr_peak", "net_new_mrr_trough"],
      "anchor": "chart_mrr_over_time",
      "text": "The chart above traces both monthly net new MRR and its running cumulative sum through 2024. The period's high-water mark arrived in $finding:net_new_mrr_peak.period at $finding:net_new_mrr_peak.value, while the softest month landed in $finding:net_new_mrr_trough.period at $finding:net_new_mrr_trough.value — a spread that illustrates the month-to-month variability sitting beneath the broader upward trend. By the final observation in $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_period, monthly net new MRR stood at $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_value, sitting $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.pct_from_peak from its peak of $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.peak_value recorded in $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.peak_period."
    },
    {
      "op": "TREND",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_split_comparison"],
      "text": "Splitting the year at its midpoint makes the acceleration concrete: the first half posted a median net new MRR of $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.early_median across $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.early_n months ($finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.early_span), while the second half reached $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.late_median — a $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.multiplier multiple — over $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.late_n months ($finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.late_span)."
    },
    {
      "op": "TREND",
      "refs": ["new_mrr_trend", "expansion_mrr_trend", "churn_mrr_trend"],
      "text": "Beneath the headline, each MRR component has its own trajectory: new MRR is trending $finding:new_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:new_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, expansion MRR is moving $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, and churn MRR is tracking $finding:churn_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:churn_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month — the combination of growing inflows and a churn trajectory that has not outpaced them explains the net positive slope."
    },
    {
      "op": "NOTE",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_step_change"],
      "text": "No persistent single-month step change in net new MRR survived the detection gates, meaning the upward trend reflects a gradual build rather than one discrete inflection point."
    },
    {
      "op": "SHAPE",
      "refs": ["mrr_annual_decomposition"],
      "text": "Across all of 2024, new MRR contributed $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.new_mrr_contribution, expansion added $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.expansion_mrr_contribution, and churn pulled $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.churn_mrr_drag — with $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.dominant as the dominant driver of the year's net result; because these three components fully account for the annual net MRR, no residual remains unexplained."
    },
    {
      "op": "EXPLAIN",
      "refs": ["segment_heterogeneity"],
      "anchor": "chart_mrr_by_plan",
      "text": "The plan-level heatmap above reveals that net new MRR differs significantly across Enterprise, Pro, and Starter plans — the heterogeneity test ($finding:segment_heterogeneity.test, p = $finding:segment_heterogeneity.p_value) confirms these are not interchangeable contributors to the trend, and the group sizes ($finding:segment_heterogeneity.group_ns) show each plan had meaningful representation throughout the period."
    },
    {
      "op": "CALLOUT",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_current_state"],
      "text": "The gap between the current level ($finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_value in $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_period) and the full-year peak ($finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.peak_value in $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.peak_period) — currently $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.pct_from_peak away — is the single most actionable number in this dashboard: closing it would require understanding which plan segment drove the peak and whether that dynamic is recoverable."
    },
    {
      "op": "METHOD",
      "refs": ["grain_check", "net_new_mrr_trend", "cumulative_mrr_trend", "mrr_annual_decomposition", "segment_heterogeneity"],
      "text": "All trend directions were estimated via OLS over monthly plan-level rows confirmed at the expected grain ($finding:grain_check.rows rows, $finding:grain_check.months months, $finding:grain_check.plans plans); component contributions were summed annually across all plans, and between-plan differences were tested using $finding:segment_heterogeneity.test dispatch based on distributional properties."
    },
    {
      "op": "CONCLUSION",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_trend", "net_new_mrr_current_state", "mrr_annual_decomposition"],
      "text": "MRR is on a $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.direction trend through 2024, adding $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, driven primarily by $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.dominant; the latest reading of $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_value sits $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.pct_from_peak below the year's peak, leaving meaningful upside if the conditions behind that peak can be identified and sustained."
    }
  ]
}
